	(footprint "curve-tracer:PinSocket_2x19_P2.54mm_Vertical_NucleoCarrier"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "d3bbd422-2be2-41a8-995f-c73572dbec2a")
		(at 107.71 50.16)
		(descr "2x19 2.54 mm socket for carrying an ST Nucleo-64 on its morpho headers (CN7/CN10), socket on the carrier top side. Pad numbering is the mirror of Connector_PinSocket_2.54mm:PinSocket_2x19_P2.54mm_Vertical: pin 2 at +2.54 mm, matching the Nucleo pins seen from above (KiCad template STM32_Nucleo-64_Morpho, UM1724 Table 26). The stock socket would connect every pin to the wrong column. The stock 3D model is reused with a +2.54 mm x offset so its body sits over the mirrored pads. hardware/DECISIONS.md L-2.")
		(tags "Nucleo morpho socket carrier mirrored")
